6. Credentials you should change afterwards
-------------------------------------------
The installer sets the root password and Wi-Fi credentials you pass on the
command line, and those end up in shell history and in the device's
configuration. Afterwards, treat the device's serial number as sensitive too:
on the *stock* firmware the per-device root password is derivable from the label
serial (see V3 in the advisory's `secondary-findings.md`). None of that applies
to the installed OpenWrt system, where the root password is the one you set.

